# 📊 Final Comparison: RBAC vs DaemonSet

| RBAC | DaemonSet |
|---|---|
| Kubernetes authorization mechanism | Kubernetes workload controller |
| Manages permissions | Manages Pods on nodes |
| Controls resource access | Ensures node-level workloads run |
| Uses Roles and Bindings | Uses DaemonSet manifests |
| Improves security | Supports node-level operations |

# 🎯 Key Takeaways

### RBAC

- RBAC controls who can perform actions on Kubernetes resources.
- Roles and RoleBindings manage namespace permissions.
- ClusterRoles and ClusterRoleBindings support cluster-wide access.
- ServiceAccounts provide identities for applications.
- Always follow least privilege.

### DaemonSet

- DaemonSet runs Pods on every eligible or selected node.
- It is commonly used for logging, monitoring, networking, and security.
- It automatically handles newly added eligible nodes.
- It does not use a replicas field.
- It is different from a Deployment.

